message.content:
Here’s how you would invoke the `XMLNamespaceBinder_endElement` function with the specified qualified name and augmentation information:

```java
// Create the QName for the element that is ending
QName element = new QName(
    "http://www.example.com",   // namespaceURI
    "item",                     // localPart
    "ex"                        // prefix
);

// Call the function with the QName and the augmentations string
functions.XMLNamespaceBinder_endElement({
    element: element,
    augs: "augmentations"
});
```

This call signals the end of the `<ex:item>` element (in the `http://www.example.com` namespace) while passing along the augmentation data `"augmentations"` to the underlying XML processing logic.

